  "reason": "The qualified_original relation 'determines_direction_and_magnitude_for_reduction' explicitly includes the directional component ('direction') required to reduce error. The qualified_proposal relation 'controls' is defined as determining or regulating only the 'magnitude'. By omitting 'direction', the proposal fails to preserve the substantive distinction present in the source text regarding the vector nature of gradients (which specify both how much and which way to update weights). While the causal strength and endpoints are compatible, the scope of the proposed relation is narrower than the original, making them non-equivalent."
